<title>INDIA: Indian soybean prices steady on limited arrivals.</title>
<headline>Indian soybean prices steady on limited arrivals.</headline>
<dateline>INDORE, India 1997-04-10</dateline>
<text>
<p>Indian soybean prices were steady Thursday in central Indian markets on limited arrivals, dealers said.</p>
<p>They said farmers and traders held back stocks to get better prices and business volumes were low with a steady undertone.</p>
<p>Soyoil prices declined on increased selling from plants and refineries, dealers said. Soyoil solvent fell 200 rupees and soyoil refined 100 rupees per tonne in light trade.</p>
<p>Soymeal and rapeseed extraction prices decreased in FOR trading. Soymeal yellow was $318 per tonne FAS (Free alongside ship) in bulk for export. Rapeseed extraction was $118 per tonne FAS (Free alongside ship) in bulk for export and was 4,150 rupees per tonne in FOR (Free on rail) condition.</p>
